// A `Cell<T>` carries its value type statically (generic extern types, higher-order-abi H4):
// `cell.new(1)` is a `Cell<int>`, so `.set("x")` is rejected at check time exactly as a signal's
// typed `set` is — the receiver's type argument seeds the method signature's variable.
// expect: error E0007 at 8:1
// expect: exit 1
use std.{cell}
c = cell.new(1)
c.set("not an int")
